session:pr592Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Continuing the #591 investigation, the user clarified the real Dexpi2Imf flow: imf:adjacentTo is not asserted directly, it is inferred by the IMF OWL ontology (owl2rl2datalog-generated rules) before the custom noaka_boundary.datalog rules ever consume it. PR #590's two tests had treated adjacentTo as a plain EDB fact, which did not match this detail. Wrote a third test deriving adjacentTo from a lower-level connectedVia relation via its own earlier-stratum rule (mirroring an OWL-RL-generated rule), keeping the rest of the scenario (select internal node, mark boundary, remove boundary again) identical to the already-passing negation-edge test. It also passed against the full-rebuild oracle, further narrowing the datalog crate's core apply_deletions algorithm out as the likely bug location. While reading sparql_endpoint/src/rules_endpoint.rs to understand how a real deployment would combine OWL-RL rules with custom datalog rules, found a genuine, documented footgun worth surfacing regardless of whether it is the active bug: POST /{dataset}/rules is a full-ruleset-replace on every call, discarding the previous ruleset and stripping all derived facts to extensional-only before rebuilding under the new rules -- if the IMF ontology's rules and the custom rules are ever loaded via two separate calls to this endpoint rather than one combined body, the second call silently wipes the first ruleset. Posted this as an update to issue #591 rather than filing a new issue, since it is a lead to check against the actual deployment's rule-loading sequence, not yet a confirmed bug." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:592 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr592 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
